@TGT
Feature: a feature file whose every scenario is coded for it

  THE REMEDY TREE for @SCN-STG-011's @integration arm — byte-for-byte its sibling
  `scn-tags-foreign-code` with the one offending id re-coded to the file it is written
  in. `@SCN-ZZZ-001` became `@SCN-TGT-002`; nothing else moved.

  The pair is what makes the arm load-bearing: red then green over one tag's difference,
  rather than a single assertion that could pass for any reason. It is also what proves
  the rule is about the DISAGREEMENT between an id and a header rather than about the
  file, the scenario count, or the shape of anything in it.

  @unit @SCN-TGT-001
  Scenario: a scenario whose code names the file it is written in
    Given the target source

  @unit @SCN-TGT-002
  Scenario: a second scenario, likewise coded for the file it is written in
    Given the target source
